.git
# Both venv paths: training/.venv is the host/manual one (training/README.md), .venv-container
# the one atlas-trainer bootstraps (docker-compose.yml's TRAINING_VENV_DIR). Neither belongs in
# any image, and at ~1.2GB the container one dominates the build context if left in — the main
# Dockerfile only COPYs go.mod/go.sum/cmd/internal, so this is purely about not shipping a gig of
# site-packages to the daemon on every build.
training/.venv
training/.venv-container
training/data
training/models
*.onnx
__pycache__
.env
.env.*
.impeccable
.claude

# Same reasoning as the venvs: a local pg_dump from rehearsing deploy/RUNBOOK.md's restore
# procedure is easily gigabytes, and nothing in any image reads one.
*.dump

# Build output that would otherwise be copied into the builder and then ignored.
*.test
coverage.out
